  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Basically, imagine a setting inside of the new IK settings that that allows the checkable option of \"IK Smoothing\" or \"IK Stabilization\" once checked will allow more settings to be visible.  Like a slider to allow how much smoothing you would like, and how much movement will be filtered. This would make stuff like movement with 3 points tracking and fullbody tracking look a LOT smoother and crisp  . Giving more realism rather then the slight janky tracking we see. This would also help with people who have medical conditions or just really shaky hands. It would allow them to have a better user experience and navigating the menu would be a lot easier if your hands didn't shake.",
